The executable first page, on a Mac without RTLD_MAIN_ONLY.

RTLD_MAIN_ONLY and getsegmentdata are later additions. Without them the
lowest accessible address is one page, which is what every non-Darwin
system uses here.

--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/WTFConfig.cpp	2026-09-23 00:27:24
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/WTFConfig.cpp	2026-09-23 00:27:24
@@ -157,7 +157,10 @@
     // FIXME: We should do a placement new for Config so we can use default initializers.
     []() -> void {
         uintptr_t onePage = pageSize(); // At least, first one page must be unmapped.
-#if OS(DARWIN)
+// Finding the executable's __PAGEZERO needs RTLD_MAIN_ONLY and
+// getsegmentdata, neither of which a Mac had this far back. One page is the
+// answer every other system gives, and is what this falls through to.
+#if OS(DARWIN) && !CP_OLD_DARWIN
 #ifdef __LP64__
         using Header = struct mach_header_64;
 #else
